A||||1||94ZonCrack||4.1 in a fiero ... valve springs ?||||5||
Z||000000||94ZonCrack||04-30-2001||03:08 PM||||I have a 4.1L from a 87 Caddilac. I'm trying to get the intake off. This thing is wierd. It appears that the pushrods go through the intake. So I have to take apart the valetrain to get the intake off? <P>I have heard the springs have to be compressed to take them off. I have never done this so do I just need a spring compressor from autozone or or something?<P>Thanks for the help. <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||04-30-2001||06:18 PM||||You need to remove the pushrods to get the intake off, but that doesn't require removing the valve springs. Just remove the bolts that hold the rocker shaft to the head, and then remove the rockers and pushrods. Be sure to follow the proper sequence for re-torquing the inake bolts when you reassemble it. If you want to remove the valve springs to replace the valve stem seals, a standard valve spring compressor will work.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
